      "note": "The classifier logs were written 2026-04-19 23:05:07+00 to 2026-04-19 23:19:43+00 and the detector logs 2026-03-05 19:28:49+00 to 2026-03-05 19:48:52+00; the windows do not overlap, so the two sides come from different runs. 35 of 35 classifier log sets (dataset x sample rate) and 7 of 7 detector log sets were written while another set of the same side was being written, so other GPUs were likely busy at the same time, sharing CPUs and PCIe. Describe these as timings from the pipeline's existing logs on the evaluation server; \"same hardware\" needs a matched, synchronized re-timing of both models on one idle GPU.",
      "paper": "Section 7 (Hardware): dual Intel Xeon Gold 6248, 504 GB RAM, and one NVIDIA Quadro RTX 6000 (24 GB).",
      "recorded_in_logs": "Not recorded. No runtime log (p002 detection_runtime.jsonl, p020 runtime.jsonl, the p121 tables) and no worker log under /polyis-cache/LOGS names a host or GPU (checked 2026-10-26)."
    },
    "inference_spikes": "A batch whose inference interval exceeds 10x its run's median is a spike. Spikes are counted, as in p121; inference_spikes and classify_inference_spikes give their excess over the median as a sensitivity check. last_batch_of_video counts spikes in a video's last batch, which is often partial, a shape the 16-batch warm-up (the first video's last full batch) does not cover; that cause is not verified.",
